Journey: Claim lifecycle across MyCover, ClaimDesk, Kafka, e-mail, the nightly batch and the PDF statement
Id: claim-lifecycle-cross-app
Tags: @e2e @cross-app @critical @kafka @email @batch @documents
Risk: 5
Requirements: E2E-1, FNOL-1, ADJ-1, EVT-2, NOTIF-2, SETTLE-1, BATCH-1, DOC-1
Actors: customer as policyholder, adjuster as adjuster
Locks: settlement-batch
Variables: amount=3875.20, approved=3600.00
Description: Two people in two applications, plus the event bus, the mail server, the batch drop folder and the statement service, in one business journey.

Set variable incidentDate to format(addDays(today(), -4), "YYYY-MM-DD")
Set variable story to "Storm tore roof tiles off above the bedroom, run " + unique("E2E")
Generate a UK IBAN as iban
Start listening on Kafka topic "larkspur.claims.events" on events as lifecycle

# 1. The customer files the claim on the portal (actor 1)
As customer:
  Open /app/claims/new
    Expect the page contains "Make a claim"
  Select "POL-H-100231 - Home" from @ClaimForm.policy
  Select "Storm" from @ClaimForm.claimType
  Fill @ClaimForm.incidentDate with ${incidentDate}
  Fill @ClaimForm.amount with ${amount}
  Fill @ClaimForm.description with "${story}"
  Upload "fixtures/kitchen-water-damage.png" to @ClaimForm.documents
  In the "Declaration" frame
    Check the "I agree to the declaration" checkbox
    Click the "Confirm declaration" button
      Expect the page contains "Declaration confirmed."
  End
  Click the @ClaimForm.submit button
    Expect the page contains "submitted"
  Capture the text of css=h1 matching "CLM-\d+" as claimId

Wait for a message in lifecycle where "$.claimId" = "${claimId}" and "$.type" = "claim.submitted" within 20 s as submitted

# 2. The adjuster approves in ClaimDesk while the customer's claim page updates by itself (both at once)
In parallel:
  As adjuster:
    Open ${BACKOFFICE_URL}/claims/${claimId}
      Expect the page contains "Review claim ${claimId}"
    Clear @ClaimDesk.approvedAmount
    Type "${approved}" into @ClaimDesk.approvedAmount
    Select "Covered in full" from @ClaimDesk.reason
    Click @ClaimDesk.approve
      Expect the page contains "Claim ${claimId} approved"
  As customer:
    Wait until testid=claim-status has text "Approved" within 30 seconds
End

# 3. The decision is published on the event bus, with the money in it
Wait for a message in lifecycle where "$.claimId" = "${claimId}" and "$.type" = "claim.approved" within 20 s matching schema "schemas/claim-event.schema.json" as approvedEvent
Capture "$.payoutAmount" from approvedEvent as payout
Get the value of query "SELECT deductible FROM policies WHERE id = 'POL-H-100231'" on claims as excess
Expect ${payout} == round(number(approved) - number(excess), 2)

# 4. The e-mail arrives with a link and a one-time code
Wait for an email to "amelia.hart@mail.larkspur.test" with subject "Claim ${claimId} approved - confirm your settlement" within 30 seconds as offer
Extract the link from ${offer} matching "/app/settlement/" as settlementLink
Extract the code from ${offer.text} matching "confirmation code is (\d{6})" as code

# 5. The customer continues from the e-mail
As customer:
  Open ${settlementLink}
    Expect the page contains "Confirm your settlement"
  Expect testid=settlement-amount shows the number "${payout}"
  Type "${code}" into the "Confirmation code" field
  Type "${iban}" into the "Bank account (IBAN)" field
  Click the "Accept settlement" button
    Expect the page contains "Settlement accepted"
Wait for a message in lifecycle where "$.claimId" = "${claimId}" and "$.type" = "settlement.accepted" within 20 s as accepted

# 6. The nightly batch pays it and the bank file lands in the drop folder
Set variable businessDate to format(today(), "YYYY-MM-DD")
Run batch job "nightly-settlement" with businessDate=${businessDate} and wait up to 2 minutes as batch
Wait for a file matching "${batch.result.fileName}" in folder "${DROP_DIR}/outbound" within 30 s as bankFile
Read the download bankFile as rows into bankRows
Run code "steps/rows.steps.ts#findRow" with rows="bankRows", column="claim_id", value="${claimId}" as paidLine
Expect ${paidLine.amount} == ${payout}
Expect ${paidLine.iban_masked} endsWith substring(iban, len(iban) - 4)
Get the first row of query "SELECT id, amount, iban FROM payments WHERE claim_id = '${claimId}'" on claims as payment
Expect ${payment.id} equals "${paidLine.payment_id}"
Expect ${payment.iban} equals "${iban}"
Wait for a message in lifecycle where "$.claimId" = "${claimId}" and "$.type" = "claim.paid" within 20 s as paid

# 7. The PDF statement matches the database (and the screen)
As customer:
  Open /app/claims/${claimId}
    Expect testid=claim-status has text "Settled"
  Capture the text of testid=claim-policy as claimPolicy
  Capture the text of testid=claim-approved as claimApproved
  Capture the text of testid=claim-payout as claimPayout
  Download the "Download statement" link as statement
  Compare document statement to the claim using statement-vs-claim and store as statementCheck
Stop listening to lifecycle
